# Line endings — all three of us develop on Windows, CI runs on Ubuntu.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores every text file as LF in the repository and checks
# it out as LF, whatever a given machine has `core.autocrlf` set to. Without
# this, one teammate's config turns a one-line change into a whole-file diff and
# the review is unreadable.
#
# This applies to files as they are written from here on. Existing files are
# already stored LF, so nothing is rewritten by adding it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never diffed, never line-ending normalized. Normalizing a PNG
# corrupts it.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.bmp  binary
*.pdf  binary

# Not listed on purpose: *.svg. The zone map is rendered as inline SVG
# (AGENTS.md §4), so SVG is source we want to diff — it is text.
